Z||000003||fldevel||11-17-2001||02:35 PM||||um ive spanked 3.4 barettas before with a 2.8 but he was one of those kids that put so many modds on that he probibly lost about 50 horse haha and yes you can OVER mod an engine ..anyway ive driven barettas before there pretty quick but couldent handle its way out of a strait line .. i would give it a go and see who wins <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||11-17-2001||02:53 PM||||There is no such thing as a Beretta with a 3.4!  The biggest V-6 available was the 3.1.  The last couple of years ('95-'96.....maybe '94 too) had SFI 3.1 (3100) engines which resemble 3.4's, but that's it.<P>Unless someone retrofitted their Beretta it only has a 3.1 V-6.  <P>That said, it would be a close race, but like fldevel said, get a Beretta in the twisties and wave bye-bye to them!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||LoW_KeY||11-17-2001||07:54 PM||||heh.. Man I've spanked 3.3 grand-ams 92-93 models with my 2.8! and the 3.3 that I did was my friends moms grand-am. <P>He can even spank 99-01 grand-ams with the 93 model.<P>of course I'm not sure if my 2.8 was normal it had 76k when I took it out and it screamed! my dad and his friend thought I was nuts to put a 3.4 in, they said the 3.4 might not run like the 2.8.<P>Boy were they wrong  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||GTMike||11-17-2001||10:10 PM||||well i lost to a 3.1 barreta  his was a stick with custom exaust  and the 160 degree chip and stat.  he had a better reaction time off the line and got about a 5 foot jump on me.  and thats the way it stayed to the about 70 then i messed up and hit my revlimiter.  if his is an auto  them you will probably be able to take him if you are a good driver  unlike me.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||11-18-2001||03:20 AM||||A good buddy of mine has a 95 that originally had a 3100 in it, but he swapped in a 3400 (it's a direct swap, kind of like the 3.4 replacing our 2.8).<P>With the 3100, auto trans, thermomaster chip/thermostat, coil, K&N style "hot air" intake, bored throttle body (another pointless mod), and custom glass pack exhaust I think my 160k mile 2.8 was scary-close with is 90k car.  On roll-ons he'd be about dead even with me until the shift, and he'd pull a car length or so.  When I did this my exhaust was shot and my clutch slave cylinder had just started going out, so shifts weren't optimum.  With the 3400, he says he should pull on me a little, as he figures it has about 5 or 10 horse more.  After he gets the 3400 intake on, he figures a total of 15 horse increase over his 3100, if that.<P>So, not to fear.  Dead stop race, I think it'll depend on the driver, transmission, tires, and luck.  Roll ons...be careful, shift fast, and smile!  If you're not having fun, you're doing it wrong, win or lose.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
